4. The one condition: you may not sell it
-----------------------------------------

You may not sell this software.

"Sell" means any arrangement in which value is exchanged for the software
itself: a licence fee, a per-seat charge, a subscription for access to it, a
paid support contract whose subject is this code, or a listing on a
third-party marketplace.

"Sell" does not mean any of the following, all of which are expressly
allowed:

  - Charging for a product that merely uses this software, provided this
    software's source is also published under this licence.
  - Charging for hosting, operations or managed service around your
    deployment, provided this software's source is also published under
    this licence.
  - Accepting donations.
  - Charging for support, consulting or custom development work.

The test is whether the customer walks away with the software. If they do,
and they paid for it rather than for your time, that is selling.

When in doubt, publish the source and give it away.


5. Conditions
-------------

Beyond the attribution requirement in section 2 and the prohibition in
section 4, there are no conditions. You are not required to:

  - disclose that you used The Project,
  - contribute changes back,
  - use the same name,
  - use the same licence, except as you choose to sublicense under
    section 3(g),
  - pay a fee, or
  - obtain permission before publishing a fork.

You may rename it, rebrand it, and rewrite it into something unrecognisable.
Please do not misrepresent it as the Original Author's work.

If you publish a fork or a derivative, saying so is a courtesy, not an
obligation. The requirement is only that you do not imply the opposite.


